From: Harvey Bellini <harveybellini@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:27:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] S8: keep the Google client secret out of the deploy
 command line

sam deploy received -GoogleClientSecret as a parameter override, exposing it to shell history and process listings. The script now stores the value in Secrets Manager (from -GoogleClientSecretArn or an environment/prompted value written to a short-lived temp file) and passes only the secret ARN, which the template validates by pattern.
---
 infra/README.md                          |  25 ++++-
 infra/template.yaml                      |   4 +
 scripts/deploy.ps1                       | 113 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 tests/unit/test_deploy_script_secrets.py |  44 +++++++++
 4 files changed, 174 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/unit/test_deploy_script_secrets.py

diff --git a/infra/README.md b/infra/README.md
index 87a09de..e377d75 100644
--- a/infra/README.md
+++ b/infra/README.md
@@ -35,15 +35,38 @@ unverified.
 ## Deploy (only after the prerequisites above)
 
 ```powershell
+# Option A - the script stores the secret itself, reading it from the
+# environment so it never appears on a command line:
+$env:GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET = "<client secret>"
+scripts/deploy.ps1 `
+  -StackName glide `
+  -Stage prod `
+  -Region eu-west-1 `
+  -BedrockModelId "eu.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0" `
+  -GoogleClientId "<client id>"
+
+# Option B - the secret already lives in Secrets Manager:
 scripts/deploy.ps1 `
   -StackName glide `
   -Stage prod `
   -Region eu-west-1 `
   -BedrockModelId "eu.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0" `
   -GoogleClientId "<client id>" `
-  -GoogleClientSecret "<client secret>"
+  -GoogleClientSecretArn "arn:aws:secretsmanager:eu-west-1:<account>:secret:glide/google-client-secret-XXXXXX"
 ```
 
+The Google client secret is never passed as a stack parameter. The script
+stores it in Secrets Manager (name `glide/google-client-secret` by default, or
+`-GoogleSecretName`) and passes only its ARN; both Lambdas resolve the value at
+runtime. The session key is generated by the stack and also read at runtime, so
+neither value appears in a Lambda environment configuration.
+
+The deployed stage writes JSON access logs to CloudWatch, throttles the API
+(and `POST /api/demo/session` more tightly), and alarms on dead-letter-queue
+depth, worker errors, API 5xx responses, and throttling; subscribe an address
+with the `AlarmEmail` parameter. Sample tenants are never scheduled and always
+run the deterministic planner, so the public demo cannot reach Bedrock.
+
 The script exports a SAM-compatible `requirements.txt` from `uv.lock`, builds
 the frontend and the Linux Lambda bundle, validates the template, then
 deploys twice: first with a placeholder frontend origin, then with the real
